  "source": "Runabout T (data/models/runabout_t): an open 1910s-style tourer after the class of the Ford Model T (docs/new_cars_plan.md 3.1). Front-engined, rear-wheel drive through an open bevel differential, the 2.9 L side-valve four (data/engines/runabout_i4_2l9_sv.json) and a three-speed sliding-mesh manual (data/gearboxes/vintage_3mt.json; the owner chose a normal manual over the period planetary box). 700 kg, CoG high (z 0.75 m) and slightly rearward (x -0.127 m) [AS]. Tall, narrow 30 x 3.5 in clincher tyres (89 mm wide on a 21 in rim, 720 mm diameter). Brakes on the rear wheels only, as in the period (the transmission brake is folded into the rear drums); no anti-roll bars (transverse leaf springs). Layout copied from data/vehicles/car_sedan.json (controllers, clutch engagement curve, shafts, fuel tank, fluid link); geometry from the model's rig (wheel centres, radii, widths, travel = the rig's joint range). Vehicle frame origin = the centre of gravity, so attachment_local = wheel centre minus CoG, lowered by the static spring compression. Springs from the corner sprung mass at 1.80 / 1.80 Hz ride frequency, dampers 0.15 / 0.25 of critical (bump / rebound), wheel inertia 0.6 m r^2: all [D] from the [AS] masses and frequencies. Fuel tank 38 L of E5 at 0.745 kg/L, 80 % full. Clutch static capacity >= 1.2x the engine's peak torque.",
